From 7ad833cfd846da5c96b8e8531d8c812fdcb36ecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] consensus(v2): connect native state, monetary and script
 rules

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Wire Lotus V2 block/transaction validation, monetary state transitions,
chainparams, and SQLite wallet support.

Original-Commit: 4acb3d0d7a8fd44cf4298fb653962abe4d68ebdf
Original-Patch: v2/015
Split-Concern: consensus

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Retain native V2 state/monetary/VM and size-commitment consensus rules, token-input filter adapter and package notification batching. Preserve shared repaired atomic admission, resolved-coin notifications and immutable snapshot bookkeeping instead of duplicating/removing those APIs. Keep one bulk-clear definition with V2 token-input skip at this native consensus owner; retain all existing snapshot provenance guards and tests.
